Editor’s Notes

<!-- about -->
Pelu Awofeso is one of the leading names in Nigeria's domestic tourism space. His contributions to, and influence in, the industry cuts across journalism, publishing, and cultural consultancy. 

He runs wakaabout Guides, a tour operating outfit. Awofeso has written & published five (6) travel books, all focused on his travels around Nigeria. 

As an  environment advocate, he co-founded Beach Samaritans, which has worked with volunteers since 2014 to cleanup public beaches in the country. 
 
His work over the years have included promoting local and international awareness of Nigerian arts, culture and traditional architecture, among other national assets, especially as they relate to or impact on domestic tourism. 

Awofeso has been celebrated at home and abroad. In 2010, he won the CNN/ Multichoice African Journalists Awards in tourism reporting. He was named the Best Tour Guide in Nigeria at the Nigeria Tourism Awards in 2017; in 2019 he won the much coveted Best Travel Journalist in Nigeria at the Nigeria Tourism Awards.


